WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:06.430
Hey, Haru-san, we've been wondering.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:07.980
Do you have a girlfriend?

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.290
That's a secret.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.120
Aww, you're so mean.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.240
Does that mean there's hope for us?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.980
Let's go on a date.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.100
I can't do that.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.160
Why not?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.740
At least give us a chance.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.720
Why not? Because...

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.250
Twitch

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.820
I belong to him body and soul.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.430
Right, Ren?

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.510
<i>Sometimes I really wish I could curse him.</i>

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.890
Uh... Why did you hit me?

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.430
I'll be yours.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.650
<i>I genuinely wanted Haru 
to say those words, but...</i>

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.080
Go see the doctor again.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:53.900
You're so mean!

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.700
If you say something like that 
in front of customers again,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.890
I'll never forgive you.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:00.660
Why?

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.290
It's the truth, and some of 
our customers like hearing it.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.790
Okay, okay.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.310
I understand.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.980
It bothers you when I say 
it like it's a joke, right?

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.650
But you know it's true, don't you?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:21.180
I'm yours, Ren.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.180
Excuse me...

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.120
It's great that you're getting along,

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.940
but did you notice I've been 
standing here this whole time?

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.690
Yeah.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.690
You didn't even hesitate! Are you 
completely ignoring my existence?!

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.430
<i>It's already been a month since 
Haru declared he was mine.</i>

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:45.200
<i>Discussions about Haru's marriage 
meetings have stopped completely.</i>

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:50.050
Ren's the jealous type, so no 
talking about marriage meetings.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:50.720
Ack!

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.110
<i>But women still approach him.</i>

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.270
<i>The situation hasn't changed much.</i>

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.220
Hey, Natsu.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:00.830
Natsuo!

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.970
What is it, Senpai?

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.730
You really don't have anything 
to do with the other Natsu?

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.710
<i>This again?</i>

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:15.320
I told you, I have no idea who he is.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.450
I used to work with the 
other Natsu at my last job.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.120
You really think two strangers 
could look so similar?

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.060
What do you want me to do about it?

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.310
I wasn't living in Japan until this spring.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:28.870
Oh, right.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:33.130
Come to think of it, I heard the 
other Natsu used to live abroad, too.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.110
<i>He won't let it go.</i>

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.820
Ask your parents.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.200
He could be your long-lost brother.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.890
Why are you so curious about him?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.030
Since he left Kabukicho,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.470
less than 20% of his customers have returned.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.890
And he had some pretty generous customers.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.770
It's a waste.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:56.150
<i>Ah, I get it. But still...</i>

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.840
I'm not him!

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.530
N-Natsu?

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.090
Hey... Natsu, what's gotten into you?

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:10.500
My senpai at the club was mean to me.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.650
He said I may look like 
Natsu, but I'm not him.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.250
Maybe I'm not cut out for this job.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.120
Oh, poor Natsu.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.190
It's okay. Everyone loves you.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.510
You think so?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.590
Yeah, you know just how to 
make girls feel needed.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.770
The way you make me feel like 
I'm the only one for you

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.520
is nothing like the other Natsu.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:39.020
<i>The only one, huh?</i>

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.450
I brought what you asked for.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.960
Thanks, Kaidou.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.110
Hey, Ren! I was wondering why you 
were in the health care room so early.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:21.930
Are you guys delivering coffee now?

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:22.960
Just here.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.720
Normally, we don't.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.200
I'll come get the thermos after school.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.220
Okay.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.470
Old man, you look kinda tired.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.770
The day's just started.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.630
Who are you calling an old man?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.730
And I'm tired because of the 
students from your dorm!

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:42.040
Oh, right. I heard the 
third-years caused a commotion

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.890
when they tried to sneak out 
of the dorm during the night.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:49.240
I was called over because one of them broke 
a window and cut his foot on the glass.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:49.240
Aaah     Aaah     Aaah

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.980
It was a pain in the ass.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.780
Do they not need to see a doctor?

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.250
It wasn't serious.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.310
Besides, I do have a medical license.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.250
What?!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:04.250
Why are you working as a school doctor 
here when you've got a license?!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.220
What did you do?

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.510
Shut up!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.930
I have my reasons.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.010
Yeah, right!

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.510
Huh?

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.790
Kaidou, come to think of it...

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:17.520
What?

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:24.210
<i>He stopped asking me hellish questions 
about what dudes do together.</i>

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.530
<i>Did that get resolved?</i>

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:29.030
<i>Did he get tired of it? Was he... satisfied?</i>

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.010
Nah, nothing. See you tomorrow.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:37.360
Okay. Let me know if you 
want a particular bean.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.150
Huh? Where's Ren?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.090
Upstairs.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.420
He's probably studying in his room.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.920
What? Ren!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:52.430
It's already midnight.
I can't keep my eyes open.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.930
You can go to bed. I have a test coming up.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.100
Brother, did Natsuo not come by?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:01.940
He did.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.440
I gave him the album you left for... Huh?

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:09.320
You went through the trouble 
of making this for him...

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.700
It's fine.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:14.200
Natsuo's always been a contrarian.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.750
What?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.700
You're not going to sleep with us?

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:20.580
Why not?

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:24.420
Because you move too much and 
talk too loud in your sleep.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.850
Natsuo can't sleep soundly like that.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:31.600
Haru-chan, Haru-chan!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.450
Good grief.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.250
Are you sure?

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.090
It's fine.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.950
I understand how you feel.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:40.350
My parents are nice. They're good people.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.100
But it doesn't feel right when people 
call Aki and Shima my brothers.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.610
But you're different, Natsuo.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:50.660
When we first met, I was so surprised 
at how similar you were to me.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:51.610
Me, too.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.240
So I feel the most relaxed 
around you, Natsuo.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.120
I love you.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.630
Aki, Shima.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:11.130
We're going to visit Natsuo's mom now.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.300
We'll go with you.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.390
You'd make too much noise at the hospital.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.830
You can go to the nearby park,

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:22.060
but not the big one on the 
other side of the road.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.620
The traffic's too dangerous.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.350
But Haru-chan...

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.910
Be home by six. See you later.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.240
Dad, Mom!

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.080
I heard Aki and Shima were run over!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.080
No, they're fine.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.240
They just tripped because 
they were scared by a car

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.580
that made a sudden left turn.

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.990
It was just a scratch, so don't worry.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:54.090
Apparently, they were trying 
to go to the big park.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.520
Dad's lecturing them right now.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:03.390
I told them not to go the big park 
because the traffic was dangerous. Why?

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.460
They were going to look for bamboo.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:07.350
Bamboo?

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.960
July 7th is your birthday.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:14.360
They wanted to make Tanabata 
decorations for you.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:19.370
And they have wishes they 
really want granted, they said.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:22.250
What wishes?

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.620
That's a secret. Aki and Shima 
would be mad if I told you.

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:39.230
"I hope Haru-chan will 
be our brother forever."

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.700
"I hope Haru-chan will love 
me and Aki someday."

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.310
Natsuo-kun, someone just called.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.650
It was, uh... Haru-kun, I believe?

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:59.660
He said he can't come get you 
today since his brothers got hurt.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:04.410
What do you want to do? 
Want me to give you a ride home?

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.920
It's fine. I can make it home by myself.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.400
<i>I know.</i>

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.280
<i>His number one changes so easily.</i>

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.890
Aki, Shima.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:23.640
Do you want to sleep with me again?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.280
Haru?

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.460
You're still not going to sleep?

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.570
I was waiting for you.

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.460
What's that?

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.200
Something Natsuo forgot.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.480
By the way, about the twins' birthday...

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.410
I forgot to ask.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:47.550
Aki will probably want meat, 
but it's hard to tell with Shima.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.140
But they said we could just 
wish them a happy birthday...

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:51.420
We can't do that.

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.710
They got me clothes and 
shoes for my birthday,

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.910
and a new electronic dictionary 
when I started school.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:02.680
Fine. I'll do some research 
tomorrow, so go to bed.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.070
Haru...

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.890
You're suffocating me.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.860
<i>He's been sleeping well lately.</i>

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:17.190
<i>But I guess this is normal for his age.</i>

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:23.240
I'll

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.830
<i>I'm glad he stopped asking for sex after that.</i>

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:23.240
be yours

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:28.450
<i>But if that was all it took to calm him, 
I should've said it sooner.</i>

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.570
<i>But Ren hasn't used those words</i>

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:35.180
<i>to restrict me once since then.</i>

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.560
This goes down easy.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.170
It's Hawaiian Kona coffee.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:45.220
Most of what we make these days is this.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.620
Is that some, too?

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:50.730
This is Colombian Maragogipe. It's for Shima.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:54.060
When we asked him what 
he wanted for his birthday,

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.510
he said he wanted his very own coffee.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.240
Hey, it's Takamura-sensei.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:03.810
Huh? The landlord's with you?

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.770
What's up?

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:09.250
I forgot to return your thermos.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.990
The health care room was locked.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.750
We had a staff meeting.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:17.750
When I stopped by the café, your 
brother invited me to stay for dinner.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:20.120
Really? Come in, then.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.900
Oh, but...

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.020
Don't worry about it.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:24.510
I was invited, too.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.510
It's the twins' birthday today.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.070
We won't be able to eat everything ourselves.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.770
We'd appreciate it if you stayed.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:39.110
High-Class 
Wagyu Beef Umenaga

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.470
It's like a trade fair of 
domestically produced beef.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:39.060
Aki and Shima got them.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.030
I don't really understand the 
relationships those two have.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.690
A few more people will be showing up tonight,

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.150
but it's just friends and family.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.560
Don't worry about it.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:54.540
I told you, I can't tonight.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.660
I'm on a date.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.360
What? The twins' birthday?

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.170
Celebrate it yourselves.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.300
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:06.300
Huh? Hey, Haru? Haru!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.780
That little...

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.530
Is it someone's birthday?

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.870
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.940
Seemed like someone you're 
pretty close to, though.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.760
Was it family?

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.430
My cousin.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.110
Four of them are living there, 
so visiting is a pain in the ass.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.070
But it's their birthday. Why don't you go?

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:23.070
Huh?

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:28.130
I'm from the country, so I'm jealous 
of people who have family nearby.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:32.080
Also, I'm glad you answered that 
call while you were with me.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.700
Is that how you act around your family?

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.340
I imagined you as someone with a permanent 
classy smile, so I was surprised.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.160
I'll call you later.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.590
Damn it.

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.340
This is Haru's fault.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:54.150
Just look at this marbling, Haru-san!

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:57.350
Oh, my. Where did you get all this meat?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:59.800
It's a present for Aki and Shima.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:01.280
These brothers...

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.360
They're a mystery.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:06.610
Aki.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.860
You're the school doctor?

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.120
Nice to meet you. I'm Takamura.

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:14.630
I can't believe Ren asked 
you those questions.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:18.270
Oh, about how men have sex?

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:23.800
Thanks for answering our brother's questions.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:28.380
Oh, no. Thank you for inviting me today.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.390
Let's have a drink together, Doc.

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:34.140
Hey, Natsuo. Have you had dinner?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:38.500
Of course not. I can't believe you called me.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.500
Now, now.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.650
Here. Give this to the twins.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.910
Thanks, but Kiyo brought drinks.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.650
Let's drink this together.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.400
Fine, I guess.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.410
Ren, grill some for me and Natsuo.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:53.740
Got it.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.360
I'm tired of meat.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.350
Really?

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.570
We have shiitake mushrooms.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.110
You idiot!

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:00.670
Those are matsutake mushrooms!

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:05.550
By the way, a senpai of mine at my job 
won't stop bothering me about you.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.510
He keeps asking me if I'm 
related to the other Natsu.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:09.530
Huh?

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:12.960
Apparently, you had some 
pretty generous customers.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:16.870
I can't believe those customers 
disappeared when you did.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.940
There's actually a trick behind that.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:23.510
You know Kashiwagi Mikiko-san, don't you?

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.980
She's called me before.

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:29.950
Most of my customers were 
introduced to me through her.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:34.450
She's a serious celebrity. Lucky me!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:37.450
<i>This bastard... I hope he dies!</i>

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:43.460
<i>Haru's never had to work for affection.</i>

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.710
<i>He's always been surrounded 
by an endless crowd of people.</i>

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:53.590
<i>When I heard his parents died in the 
accident and he was seriously injured,</i>

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:57.990
<i>I couldn't believe that happened to him.</i>

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:04.100
<i>To the guy smiling next to me right 
now, without a care in the world.</i>

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:08.200
<i>No, wait. The reason he's like 
this now is probably because...</i>

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.610
Oh, right. The album...

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:13.610
You know Shima made it for—

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.620
Haru, the meat...

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.550
I knew it... You...

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:29.760
<i>What kind of development is this?!</i>

00:16:30.310 --> 00:16:31.610
You idiot!

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:34.470
Huh?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.870
Don't ever touch Haru again! This is mine!

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:42.980
Uh, Ren? Don't you think 
you kicked the wrong guy?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:46.980
A-Are they finally announcing 
their relationship?

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:49.980
Hey, Ren!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.360
Natsuo, that's enough joking around!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.030
You're one to talk.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.480
You're in a really good mood, aren't you?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.240
Huh?

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:03.270
What? Doesn't hearing him 
say that make you happy?

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:07.970
You owe me one.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.070
Got it.

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:12.200
This always happens.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:13.130
Yeah.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.010
<i>They just let that one go.</i>

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:19.490
Ren.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.200
How did you get into my room?

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.040
I took off the locks ages ago.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:29.390
I can't have you hiding 
in your room like this.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:31.460
Ren?

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.500
Tell the others I'm sorry for causing a fuss.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:37.030
Okay.

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.270
Anyway, could you say that again?

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:41.790
Say what?

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.580
"This is mine."

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:46.970
I didn't mean to say it.

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:49.730
I know, but I want to hear it.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.140
Say it one more time.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.800
Chomp

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:04.760
Haru, you're mine.

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:09.930
<i>As a man wanting to be 
under this child's hold,</i>

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:11.570
<i>I'm no longer his older brother.</i>

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:16.630
<i>With each passing season, 
that feeling grows stronger.</i>

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:21.200
Okay, Kaidou, open wide.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.700
Say "ahh."

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:24.880
Ahh.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.130
Your teeth look pretty good.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.710
I'm impressed.

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:33.310
Uh, doc? That's not why we're here.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:37.000
Oh, right. It's just a cold.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.940
You'll get better in a few days.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:43.400
What? But his throat is really 
swollen, and he has a fever.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:45.630
His body hurts all over, too.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.110
Bro, it's practically tradition for Ren

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.980
to catch a cold this time of year.

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:56.090
Although I can't believe he got 
sick on his own birthday this year.

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:56.990
What?!

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.860
It's your fault for dragging Ren to the 
convenience store when he's so lightly dressed!

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.830
I didn't force him to come!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.620
He just followed me because 
I said I'd buy him ice cream!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.070
Yeah, that's it!

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:10.430
How can you feed that 
stuff to Ren every night?!

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:15.310
<i>Nothing good ever comes from 
associating with these brothers.</i>

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.130
Think you can eat anything?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.110
No, I'll pass.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:25.140
If you're sick, we'll have to 
postpone tonight's party.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:29.890
It's Christmas. Party as hard as you want.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.840
I don't care about Christmas.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:35.970
It's more important that 
today's your birthday.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:39.020
You're exaggerating. I'm going to sleep.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:40.150
You're no fun.

00:19:41.230 --> 00:19:41.990
Ren.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:44.490
Happy birthday.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:48.660
I'm glad I got to spend your 
birthday by your side again.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.660
You got a card from Rob and Haruko-san.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.630
I'll leave it here.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.130
<i>He beat me to it again.</i>

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.680
<i>I was going to say that.</i>

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:05.680
<i>Two years ago, this day 
was nothing but painful.</i>

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.010
<i>I told Haru how I felt,</i>

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:12.300
<i>prepared to return to Canada alone.</i>

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:17.190
<i>Being apart from Haru was too painful.</i>

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:21.960
<i>I should tell Haru later 
that I feel the same way.</i>

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.620
Haru?

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.310
You're awake, Ren?

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:34.410
Are you hungry? I made some rice porridge.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.880
I don't need any. I'm thirsty.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:38.880
Here, water.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.420
You still have a fever.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:43.410
Does it hurt?

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.620
No, I'm just sleepy.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.890
Anyway, Haru, there's something 
I want to tell you.

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:51.890
Tell me?

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:55.900
I'm glad we're together, too.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.050
Ren...

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:58.990
Also...

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.200
They're pregnant.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:05.790
But they don't know who the father is.

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:09.910
We'll have to think about names...

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:14.260
<i>What's going on with this kid?!</i>

00:22:56.720 --> 00:22:58.520
They decided on names for the kids?

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:02.520
Yeah, Shima named them after goddesses.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:05.650
They're Urd, Skuld, and Ver.

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:10.000
Uh, wouldn't something Japanese be better?

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:11.850
Like Aiko or Sakura.

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:13.160
It's already been decided.

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:16.090
What? But there are plenty of other names.

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:17.710
Apparently he still hasn't 
realized they're puppies.

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:20.220
There's Yuki, Ayumi, Aya, Noriko...

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.220
This is too stupid.

00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:22.920
Ren, what about Kana or Yuka?

00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:25.140
Junko or Tomo could be good, too.

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:26.430
Shut up!

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:40.240
Thank you for watching.
